## Why This Is Asked

A practical UX feature tests offline resilience, local storage usage, and simple cross-tab conflict handling without server changes.

## Key Concepts

- Debounce autosave
- localStorage vs IndexedDB
- Versioning for conflict detection
- Cross-tab synchronization basics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal autosave scaffold
let timer;
function onChange(content){
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(()=> {
     const note = { content, lastSaved: Date.now(), version: (NOTE_VERSION++) };
     localStorage.setItem('noteDraft', JSON.stringify(note));
  }, 300);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test offline reload and cross-tab conflict?
- How would you handle storage quota and large notes?

## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?

## Why This Question Is Asked
